# Error handling and observability
- Follow `docs/HiveForYou-ERROR-HANDLING-OBSERVABILITY.md` for public error shape, stages, codes, and logging rules.
- Use `@hiveforyou/contracts` for allowlisted error codes/categories/stages and `toPublicErrorResponse()`.
- Resolve or generate `x-correlation-id` at the API boundary; return it on responses and error JSON.
- Emit one structured JSON log event per meaningful transition at the owning boundary; allowlisted fields only; never log document text, quotes, prompts, tokens, or credentials.
- Map unexpected exceptions, including partial lookalike objects, to `INTERNAL_ERROR` with a safe message. Keep `cause` non-enumerable and out of public JSON. Do not expose stacks, paths, or provider bodies to clients or logs.
- Do not add retry/timeout frameworks, observability vendors, diagnostic env vars, or fail-only public routes without an approved ticket need.
